.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt BIGD 5
.Os "BioZig Systems"
.Sh NAME
.Nm bigd
.Nd binary problem instance format for BIG-LL evolutionary search
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa filename.bigd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file format is a compact, little-endian, 64-byte cacheline-aligned binary
container format specifically designed for storing combinatorial optimization
instances evaluated by the
.Xr big-ll 1
evolutionary engine and
.Xr libbig_ll 3
library.
.Pp
By strictly maintaining 64-byte alignment for both the container header and
subsequent data payloads,
.Nm
files can be mapped directly into user space via
.Xr mmap 2
and passed directly to Apple Silicon Metal GPU compute pipelines via
.Li makeBuffer(bytesNoCopy:length:options:deallocator:)
without intermediate memory copies or CPU bus re-alignment penalties.
.Sh FILE LAYOUT
A
.Nm
file consists of a mandatory 64-byte header immediately followed by contiguous
payload data.
All integer and floating-point fields are encoded in standard little-endian byte
order.
.Ss Binary Header Structure
The first 64 bytes of the file are structured as follows:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
Offset  Size  Type       Field Name             Description
------------------------------------------------------------------------
0x00    4     char[4]    magic                  Magic bytes: "BIGD"
0x04    2     uint16_t   version_major          File format major version (1)
0x06    2     uint16_t   domain_id              Problem domain identifier
0x08    4     uint32_t   chromosome_bits        Chromosome bit width (L)
0x0C    4     uint32_t   word_count             64-bit word count (W = L / 64)
0x10    8     uint64_t   seed_salt              PRNG initialization salt
0x18    8     uint64_t   primary_payload_len    Primary payload size in bytes
0x20    8     uint64_t   secondary_payload_len  Secondary payload size in bytes
0x28    8     double     target_fitness         Reference or optimal fitness
0x30    16    uint8_t[16] reserved              Reserved padding (zero-filled)
0x40    ...   bytes      payload_data           Contiguous domain data
.Ed
.Ss Header Field Details
.Bl -tag -width "chromosome_bits"
.It Va magic
A 4-byte ASCII signature:
.Ql B , Ql I , Ql G , Ql D
.Pq 0x42 0x49 0x47 0x44 .
Parsers must reject any file whose leading 4 bytes do not match this magic
sequence.
.It Va version_major
The format specification major version.
Current specification version is 1.
.It Va domain_id
Identifies the mathematical problem domain and the semantic structure of the
payload:
.Bl -tag -width "3" -compact
.It 1
Finance (Markowitz Mean-Variance Portfolio Optimization).
.It 2
Telecom (5G/6G MIMO Multi-User Beamforming & Power Allocation).
.It 3
Bioinformatics (Molecular Contact Map & Conformation Search).
.It 4
Aerospace (Constellation Satellite Scheduling & Orbital Debris Avoidance).
.El
.It Va chromosome_bits
The problem dimensionality
.Ar L ,
representing the number of binary decision variables in each candidate solution.
Must be strictly greater than zero and an integer multiple of 64.
Standard benchmark instances typically evaluate
.Ar L
in {256, 512, 1024, 2048, 4096}.
.It Va word_count
The number of 64-bit unsigned integers required to represent a single candidate
bitboard
.Pq Ql W = chromosome_bits / 64 .
.It Va seed_salt
A 64-bit unsigned integer used to seed synthetic problem generators or record
the pseudo-random sequence identifier of the instance.
.It Va primary_payload_len
The size in bytes of the primary data payload starting at offset 0x40
(byte 64).
.It Va secondary_payload_len
The size in bytes of the secondary data payload immediately following the
primary payload.
If an instance has no secondary payload, this field is set to 0.
.It Va target_fitness
An IEEE 754 double-precision floating-point value recording the known theoretical
global optimum, mathematical upper bound, or classical heuristic baseline
score for benchmark validation.
.It Va reserved
A 16-byte zero-filled padding block ensuring that the total header length is
exactly 64 bytes (the native L1/L2 cacheline size of ARM64 and x86_64).
.El
.Sh DOMAIN PAYLOAD SPECIFICATIONS
Payload data begins immediately at byte offset 64
.Pq 0x40 .
Its internal layout depends on
.Va domain_id :
.Ss Domain 1: Finance (Markowitz QP)
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Primary Payload :
Expected asset return vector
.Sm off
.Pf \(mu \(in R^L
.Sm on ,
stored as an array of
.Ar L
single-precision IEEE 754 floats
.Pq Ar L No * 4 bytes .
.It
.Sy Secondary Payload :
Asset covariance matrix
.Sm off
.Pf \(Sigma \(in R^{L \times L}
.Sm on ,
stored as a row-major array of
.Sm off
.Pf L \(mu L
.Sm on
single-precision floats
.Pq Ar L No * Ar L No * 4 bytes .
.It
.Sy Objective Function :
Given candidate asset selection bitboard
.Sm off
.Pf x \(in {0, 1}^L
.Sm on :
.Pp
.Dl "f(x) = dot(x, mu) - lambda * quad(x, Sigma, x) - penalty(norm_1(x) - K)"
.El
.Ss Domain 2: Telecom (MIMO Beamforming)
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Primary Payload :
Channel state transfer matrix
.Sm off
.Pf H \(in C^{M \times K}
.Sm on ,
stored as contiguous interleaved real and imaginary float32 pairs.
.It
.Sy Secondary Payload :
User Signal-to-Interference-plus-Noise (SINR) target vector and power
constraint parameters.
.El
.Ss Domain 3: Bioinformatics
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Primary Payload :
Residue-residue contact distance matrix or pairwise amino acid interaction
tensor.
.It
.Sy Secondary Payload :
Secondary structure propensity weights and solvent accessibility vector.
.El
.Ss Domain 4: Aerospace
.Bl -bullet
.It
.Sy Primary Payload :
Ground target observation reward raster.
.It
.Sy Secondary Payload :
Orbital eclipse timeline and payload slewing constraint matrices.
.El
.Sh HARDWARE CONSIDERATIONS AND ZERO-COPY MAPPING
Because
.Nm
guarantees that:
.Bl -enum
.It
The file size is a multiple of 64 bytes,
.It
The header is exactly 64 bytes, and
.It
Payload data types are aligned to their natural word boundaries,
.El
.Pp
operating systems can map
.Nm
files directly into memory using
.Xr mmap 2 .
On Apple Silicon, host virtual memory pages backed by an
.Nm
file can be shared directly with Metal compute shaders via the unified DRAM
fabric:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
// Zero-copy Metal buffer initialization in Swift / Objective-C
let buffer = device.makeBuffer(
    bytesNoCopy: mmapPointer.advanced(by: 64),
    length: payloadLength,
    options: .storageModeShared,
    deallocator: nil
)
.Ed
.Sh UTILITIES
The
.Xr big-ll 1
utility provides dedicated subcommands for manipulating
.Nm
files:
.Bl -tag -width "big-ll generate-suite"
.It Cm big-ll inspect Ar file.bigd
Displays metadata, payload lengths, and target fitness for
.Ar file.bigd .
.It Cm big-ll generate Ar domain Ar out.bigd
Generates a synthetic instance for the specified domain.
.It Cm big-ll generate-suite Op Ar target_dir
Generates a full benchmark suite across standard dimensions.
.It Cm big-ll ingest-real Op Ar raw_dir Op Ar out_dir
Compiles external raw CSV/NumPy datasets into aligned
.Nm
files.
.El
